From 438090b9262225c84d72617bba300a085d72f131 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:56:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CPU-features CF1: SMEP/SMAP made true, then advertised

The walk guards for CR4.SMEP/SMAP sat inside the supervisor-page
branch of translate(): a kernel that set either bit faulted on its
own text while user pages stayed open. Invisible since the
original upstream code because CPUID advertised neither feature,
so no consumer ever enabled them and no test ever vectored them.

- Guards moved to supervisor-accesses-of-user-pages with the
  architected error codes (SMEP P|I/D, SMAP P/P|W); user_cpl
  already folds K4's desc_sv rule, so implicit descriptor
  accesses take the same gate (QEMU's kernel-index shape). The
  P2 TLB needed nothing: CR4/CPL/AC/desc_sv/mode were already
  its key, proven by the warm STAC->CLAC toggle vector.
- Gate delivery now clears EFLAGS.AC alongside IF (the frame
  preserves the old bit for IRET); page_fault sets I/D for SMEP
  regardless of NXE (the two nx_hit sites only).
- Second latent defect in the same site: STAC/CLAC had no break
  and fell through into decode_modrm + the SIDT store at linear
  address 0, overwriting the guest's first bytes with the IDT
  pseudo-descriptor on every execution. The cases now end, and
  CPL>0 takes the delivered architected #UD.
- CPUID leaf 7 advertises SMEP|SMAP|ERMS, pinned in
  test_cpuid_leaves. AuraLite-OS now lights its SMEP/SMAP
  receipts and STAC/CLAC copy paths up on this machine.

Vectors: 9 in tests/test_tlb.c::smep_smap (own supervisor-mapped
fixture; CF0 repro table in house form, linear-0 canary, CPL3
#UD, AC across delivery). NC against 86539e4: 11 pre-existing P2
vectors pass, the first CF1 case aborts in smstep on the inverted
walk's bogus supervisor-fetch #PF; test-unit aborts on the leaf-7
assertion. Gates: make test and make test-sanitize green with
both live SeaBIOS ISO lanes; no firmware receipt delta.
